cute renal injury and renal failure</article-title><source>Shock</source><year>2006</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>253</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16912649</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.shk.0000225415.5969694.ce</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chiu</surname><given-names>YJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Reid</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of phosphodiesterase III with milrinone increases renin secretion in human subjects</article-title><source>J Pharmacol Exp Ther</source><year>1999</year><volume>290</volume><fpage>16</fpage><lpage>19</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10381754</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Samikkannu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhat</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wittman</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Thekkumkara</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acute effect of high glucose on long-term cell growth: a role for transient glucose increase in proximal tubule cell injury</article-title><source>Am J Physiol Renal Physiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>291</volume><fpage>F162</fpage><lpage>F175</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16467130</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1152/ajprenal.00189.2005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leverve</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hyperglycemia and oxidative stress: complex relationships with attractive prospects</article-title><source